body:
A sealed class restricts the subclasses to the same file and package, which makes exhaustive when-expressions possible.

```kotlin
sealed class Result {
    data class Success(val value: Int) : Result()
    data class Failure(val error: String) : Result()
}

fun describe(r: Result): String = when (r) {
    is Result.Success -> "ok: ${r.value}"
    is Result.Failure -> "error: ${r.error}"
}
```

Because every subclass is known at compile time, the compiler verifies the when is exhaustive, so a new subclass forces updating every where statement that handles Result.
